Z||000006||Greg Piet||09-24-1999||01:35 AM||||I too thought about headers, but I was concerned with their comaptibility with Stroker's soon to be offered turbo kit.<BR>It seems it would be a shame to put on headers that would have to be removed if one was going to put in a turbo kit soon.<P>The term cheap headers kind of confuses me, since I kind of believe in the expression "speed is just a question of money...  How fast do you want to go?"<BR>When I saw how expensive stock manifolds were, I just assumed headers would be above that price.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fieroshop||09-24-1999||02:52 AM||||I also think that headers are too expensive so I tell my customers that they can get almost as much horsepower increase by having the exhaust manifolds ported. It works I know I did it to my 88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||mwbackus||09-24-1999||03:13 AM||||Ya, I would say they are way too expensive.. You can get Edelbrock headers for an S-10 pickup (a damn 4000 lb truck!!) with the same 2.8 block for less than $200.  It just isn't fair.. :Þ<P>Mike <BR>(who is really mad at the aftermarket performance parts industry for thumbing their noses at our cars!)||||reg||1
Z||000009||DXR_WILL||09-24-1999||06:28 AM||||I wouldn't waste my money on those expensive headers.  Re-welled and port your stock manifold.  My dad has them on his SE, and I do feel a bit of a difference.  It's also a hell of a lot cheaper as well.||||reg||1
