Z||000022||fastonpumpgas||09-25-1999||08:14 AM||||i gues I will end up ordering some from the fiero store, I mean I have put nothing but the top stuff in my 3.1 so far, why skimp now.  Bu tthat is a kick in the *ss.  I haope I get the gains I want, I dont like the turbo idea or supercharged. I am trying to do this the old way.  Might get greedy and put those forged piston to use, if I see possible 14's though ||||reg||1
Z||000023||batboy||09-25-1999||08:55 AM||||FastGas, I hear you about building an engine the old fashion way. You're a man who thinks like me. I know those headers are expensive, but anything you do to help that engine flow is a good thing. Some careful pocket porting in the heads, the right cam, and free flowing exhaust all help flow which of course translates to more power. If I had forged pistons in a 2.8/3.1, I might be tempted to buy a 70 shot NOS system, just in case ya need it. **wink, wink**||||reg||1
Z||000024||DXR_DAD||09-26-1999||09:26 PM||||Just found a good write-up in August 1999 <BR>Car Craft "Headers vs Manifolds" Can manifolds be ported for stealth power? They are talking about iron manifolds but I thought it was good how they hone the manifold. Extrude Hone is the company that does this process. If you can check this out!||||reg||1
Z||000025||BlackGT||09-30-1999||10:42 AM||||Well I need to throw my 0.02 in...<BR>I`m in the process of having my stock manifolds reinforced welded and when I get them back I will start the grinding process<BR>over the weekend. I drove my friends 87GT with those sprint headers from the Fiero store and I didn`t feel a big difference! He agrees with me and feels that he should have done what I`m doing. It`s a heluva lot cheaper and you get the same performance gains!!!||||reg||6
Z||000026||DXR_DAD||09-30-1999||10:01 PM||||Well.....That makes 0.04. Iam with you on this one BlackGT||||reg||14
